WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.680
Good morning John, and good morning to the class of 2017

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.500
and also all of the other classes and people who aren't in classes.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.000
Here's what I think is probably up with most of you, it's what was up with me,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
you have done the thing other people have told you to do for your entire life

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.740
and now you don't know what to do

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.870
because guess what? Freedom is awful and

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.180
I can't decide what to have for dinner,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.780
much less what to do with the rest of my life.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.380
You have an infinite number of paths ahead of you, pick!

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.660
Join the army or the Peace Corps or the clergy.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:30.118
Go to grad school or business school or a horoscope school, where astrologers go to school?

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.000
Do your side hustles and start a podcast and follow your dreams,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.000
until you realize that your dreams aren't actually that great

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.500
because work is much more to do with the people you do it within your own attitude than whatever it is you're actually doing.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:45.040
I love science, and I got a job doing science after I graduated and it was miserable.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.200
Not because I didn't like the science,

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.460
it's because I was the only person in the lab.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.940
All the time, just me and my pipettes and a family of armadillos and a giant canister of liquid nitrogen,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.010
and yes, that sounds kind of awesome.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.770
But after six months, it's a little lonely.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:03.800
If you are very lucky, you have discovered something you like doing.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.720
It is very easy to get through life without discovering a salable skill that you enjoy,

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.400
and that is, by the way, how dream jobs actually happen.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.780
You find a thing that you like doing, at least most of the time,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.760
and you do it enough that you get good enough at it that people will pay you to do it.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:23.159
So, if you like doing a thing that has economic value, continue doing that thing.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.500
You are one of the lucky ones.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.560
If you don't, welcome to being most people.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.020
To you, I offer only this:

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.620
you are normal.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:36.820
We evolved for a world so unlike the one that we find ourselves in

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:40.320
that it is amazing any of us can function at all.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.340
Humans are, above everything, adaptable.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.399
But, the idea that any of this stuff --

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.880
careers and job interviews and diplomas and the jobs themselves --

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:58.110
is like a normal human construction that like, that you're designed to ta--ngh-- it's crazy!

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:06.240
It's all brand-new super weird cultural constructions that didn't exist, like 300 years ago.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.540
This stuff all seems very normal, it's not!

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.340
And if you base your self-worth on it, which we do --

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.880
we are asked to! It's what society says our value is --

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:19.060
but if you do, it's going to be real hard to be happy.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.920
You don't need a job that changes the world

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.980
and that's environmentally friendly and that is creatively fulfilling in every way

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.360
and that uses any diploma, much less the diploma that you happen to have.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.271
You need to feel valuable,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:39.000
but all of the different constraints that is being placed on like what a "valuable life" looks like -- it's not!

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.310
It's way too much to expect from anyone, much less everyone!

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.740
It takes so long to get it in your head!

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.700
You didn't go to school to learn how to get a job, you went to school to learn!

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.800
And you did it! You know more stuff now!

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:56.360
So, you might never know what you're doing, but do me this favor:

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.960
get out of bed every morning knowing that no one changes the world alone

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.300
and no one doesn't change it at all.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.520
We are all exceptional and none of us are.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.840
And we are all lost, sometimes.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.960
So follow a path -- any path -- until you get to a place that you feel like you don't like,

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.720
and then change your direction.

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:18.510
Because there's one thing that you are making every day,

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.260
no matter what you're doing,

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.860
and that is yourself.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.190
That is your job.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.684
And you must do it well.

00:03:24.684 --> 00:03:27.640
For me, there's a lot of strength in knowing

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.150
that the wandering that I am doing, that I've done

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:35.060
is normal and kind of beautiful and not something I should be stressed out about.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:39.720
You're on a path. You don't know where it's going, and that would be boring if you did.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.800
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.220
Here is the current list of people who will be at PodCon... just an update.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:49.220
podcon.com

